    "summary": "pcap-parser is a Rust library for parsing PCAP and PCAP-NG network capture file formats. The architecture centers on a core library layer that defines common types (link types, error types, endianness handling, block enumerations) and abstract traits for capture reading. Two parallel internal modules implement format-specific parsing: one for the legacy PCAP format and one for the more modern PCAP-NG format with its rich set of block types (section headers, interface descriptions, enhanced packets, name resolution, decryption secrets, etc.). A data layer provides additional parsers for specific link-layer payload formats like NFLOG and Exported PDU. Serialization support allows writing parsed structures back to binary. The project includes comprehensive integration tests and benchmarks backed by sample capture files, an example binary for inspecting capture files, and standard Rust CI/CD infrastructure."
  },
